WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.770
Fight for your justice,
show your courage.

00:06.770 --> 00:10.370
Right! Grasp truth in these hands.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.780
Fight for your justice, I want you

00:13.780 --> 00:21.200
as you fight through
with your head held up high.

00:35.860 --> 00:39.930
Rather than polishing diamonds

00:43.040 --> 00:46.970
give me a glistening future.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.480
Even if nothing's there, get up.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.350
It's important to turn on the switch.

00:57.450 --> 01:00.220
Something new that I don't want to yield.

01:00.220 --> 01:04.750
Seeking it is justice!

01:06.360 --> 01:09.930
Fight for your justice,
be serious about it.

01:09.930 --> 01:13.540
Right! Face reality head on.

01:13.540 --> 01:16.940
Fight for your justice,
I love how you

01:16.940 --> 01:27.340
never give up even if
the current is against you.

01:43.400 --> 01:46.430
You're looking better now.

01:46.430 --> 01:47.600
Stop that...

01:47.600 --> 01:49.730
Nothing comes out of complimenting me.

01:51.770 --> 01:53.780
Y-You know...

01:53.780 --> 01:57.710
I thought I'd say thanks to you...

01:58.710 --> 02:01.720
For when I first fought on this thing.

02:01.720 --> 02:04.150
It's because of what you said back then

02:04.150 --> 02:06.960
that I've been able to live to this day.

02:06.960 --> 02:11.760
It's kinda pathetic,
but I couldn't put up proof that I existed.

02:11.760 --> 02:15.230
But you gave me
a chance to start thinking

02:15.230 --> 02:18.830
instead of being
the forceful loser I was.

02:18.830 --> 02:20.490
Thanks.

02:22.470 --> 02:24.040
I assure you.

02:24.040 --> 02:27.500
Everything you've done up till now
is proof of Hibiki Tokai's existence.

02:34.150 --> 02:35.820
Dita.

02:35.820 --> 02:37.150
Misty!

02:37.150 --> 02:40.660
It's finally time...
I thought I'd give some encouragement.

02:40.660 --> 02:42.490
Thanks.

02:42.490 --> 02:43.860
Are you afraid?

02:43.860 --> 02:47.660
No, I'm all right
since I'm with Mr. Alien.

02:47.660 --> 02:50.100
I can't beat your natural high, Dita...

02:50.100 --> 02:53.100
I think Mr. Alien is really amazing.

02:53.100 --> 02:55.700
Because he's trying so hard.

02:55.700 --> 02:59.170
He screws up a lot...
and gets mad easily...

02:59.170 --> 03:02.380
but it always seems like
he'll do something amazing.

03:02.380 --> 03:04.780
It makes me worry when I watch him...

03:04.780 --> 03:07.550
but when I'm with him,
my heart is racing.

03:07.550 --> 03:10.380
That's why I can do my best.

03:12.920 --> 03:14.060
Sheesh...

03:14.060 --> 03:16.960
How long will she
say such childish things?

03:16.960 --> 03:19.530
Are you wishing for a change?

03:19.530 --> 03:22.330
You're starting to sound
more and more like Hibiki.

03:26.830 --> 03:28.500
What's wrong?

03:30.740 --> 03:34.580
I'm going to stop
checking other people, ribbit!

03:34.580 --> 03:36.540
I see.

03:36.540 --> 03:39.810
I thought I'd get
things straight for myself...

03:39.810 --> 03:40.850
That's true.

03:40.850 --> 03:43.980
I thought the same
thing after meeting you all.

03:48.060 --> 03:52.390
BC, there's a circuit
that I'd like you to open.

03:52.390 --> 03:53.700
Yes?

03:53.700 --> 03:57.000
To the bosses of men and women.

03:57.000 --> 03:59.800
To Grand Pa and Grand Ma?

04:21.390 --> 04:22.720
- Sir!
- Sir!

04:26.730 --> 04:28.160
Look at this.

04:28.160 --> 04:31.500
Something's finally sprouting,
even on this parched land.

04:31.500 --> 04:37.440
You didn't call us just to
show off something of that sort?

04:37.440 --> 04:41.440
I take it your whimsical nature
will never change until you die.

04:41.440 --> 04:43.710
That's right, Jin.

04:43.710 --> 04:47.350
It's been decades since
this line was opened.

04:47.350 --> 04:48.980
Grand Ma!

04:48.980 --> 04:53.050
Long time no see, Grand Ma...
No, my dear sister, Anri!

04:53.050 --> 04:55.520
Stop fooling around already!

04:55.520 --> 05:00.230
You volunteered to guard all
the people asleep underground!

05:00.230 --> 05:03.400
What are you thinking
after all this time?

05:03.400 --> 05:05.170
The time has come.

05:05.170 --> 05:06.530
What?

05:06.530 --> 05:07.940
100 years ago...

05:07.940 --> 05:11.410
we came all the way here
with colonization ships.

05:11.410 --> 05:13.370
And we set roots in this soil

05:13.370 --> 05:18.580
believing it would increase the
number of Earth's descendants.

05:18.580 --> 05:21.150
Jin, what are you getting at?

05:21.150 --> 05:24.820
It's about time we pulled
away from them, brothers.

05:24.820 --> 05:26.850
The future is not ours.

05:26.850 --> 05:28.520
What are you saying, Jin?

05:28.520 --> 05:33.630
It was a hard choice for
Zen Grand Pa and Anri Grand Ma to make,

05:33.630 --> 05:35.460
to separate men and women!

05:35.460 --> 05:37.130
And now you...

05:37.130 --> 05:41.300
The colonization ships
were for human prosperity.

05:41.300 --> 05:46.210
They were not for having
our bodies forcefully taken away.

05:46.210 --> 05:47.280
Am I wrong?

05:47.280 --> 05:51.750
But we can't waste everything
we've done up till now!

05:51.750 --> 05:54.380
We have sacrificed too much for that!

05:54.380 --> 05:56.050
So what?

05:56.050 --> 06:00.820
Do you think it's a reason
to force death on the children

06:00.820 --> 06:03.990
that have called this
land home just for our sake?

06:03.990 --> 06:06.330
What are you saying now?

06:06.330 --> 06:09.730
It will only be a repeat of 100 years ago!

06:09.730 --> 06:11.970
I held back then...

06:11.970 --> 06:14.000
but I won't hold back now.

06:14.000 --> 06:15.900
Then we have no answer.

06:15.900 --> 06:20.580
The eight of us only
results in a split vote!

06:20.580 --> 06:23.510
Well, is that really so?

06:29.750 --> 06:31.890
Hey, can we talk a bit?

06:31.890 --> 06:35.160
I've never went full force before...

06:35.160 --> 06:38.030
Sheesh, each and every guy today...

06:38.030 --> 06:42.300
I was always half-assed
and really cold about things...

06:42.300 --> 06:45.500
I always came up with
excuses when things failed.

06:45.500 --> 06:47.540
Me, too!

06:47.540 --> 06:50.710
Showing how stupid
you are isn't a bad thing.

06:50.710 --> 06:55.140
Having people close by who
can accept that is a good thing.

06:55.140 --> 06:57.150
Right?

06:57.150 --> 07:00.050
It really is!
Hibiki, let's have a blast!

07:00.050 --> 07:01.980
Yeah!

07:01.980 --> 07:04.690
I cannot allow denial without options...

07:04.690 --> 07:06.690
That was the way we decided things!

07:06.690 --> 07:10.220
Then I will have the
ninth one decide everything.

07:10.220 --> 07:11.430
The ninth?

07:11.430 --> 07:12.460
Hibiki.

07:12.460 --> 07:14.160
Hibiki?

07:14.160 --> 07:16.800
Impossible!

07:16.800 --> 07:19.230
Yes, it's the impossible, brother.

07:19.230 --> 07:23.540
The son of you two, Hibiki Tokai,
is striving for an answer.

07:23.540 --> 07:25.110
Why Hibiki?

07:25.110 --> 07:28.510
He should still be
in cold sleep right now.

07:28.510 --> 07:31.310
He suddenly woke up 14 years ago.

07:31.310 --> 07:35.980
Right around when you all were
starting to build the Ikazuchi.

07:35.980 --> 07:39.750
The wheels of fate started to turn.

07:39.750 --> 07:44.260
That boy Hibiki is just
about to start fighting with us.

07:44.260 --> 07:46.290
Who are you?

07:46.290 --> 07:49.200
You must be the pirate leader, Magno.

07:49.200 --> 07:50.630
Magno...

07:50.630 --> 07:52.670
Oh, so it's little Magno!

07:52.670 --> 07:54.470
What memories!

07:54.470 --> 07:58.170
Uncle Jin, you played
with me a lot on the ship.

07:58.170 --> 07:59.310
What memories.

07:59.310 --> 08:03.140
What does the leader
of the pirates want with us?

08:03.140 --> 08:05.410
I'm one of the first generation

08:05.410 --> 08:09.450
so I thought I'd give
my two cents, as well.

08:09.450 --> 08:11.950
We've made the ultimate decision...

08:11.950 --> 08:15.790
and it took us
100 years to make it happen.

08:15.790 --> 08:17.590
There's nothing to discuss.

08:17.590 --> 08:19.430
That's to your benefit!

08:19.430 --> 08:22.360
It's unrelated to the young
living that future!

08:22.360 --> 08:24.030
What insolence.

08:24.030 --> 08:26.800
Do you intend to challenge us?

08:26.800 --> 08:30.070
That's enough...

08:30.070 --> 08:32.040
We've come this far.

08:32.040 --> 08:34.040
That's something to be proud of.

08:34.040 --> 08:38.380
But we shouldn't talk so much
about the problem from here on.

08:38.380 --> 08:40.180
How about it, brothers...

08:40.180 --> 08:45.050
Shall we entrust Hibiki with our future?

08:45.050 --> 08:46.890
Gramps!

08:46.890 --> 08:48.550
Hibiki!

08:50.690 --> 08:53.060
Gramps, I have friends now!

08:53.060 --> 08:56.200
Oh, you do look a little different.

08:56.200 --> 08:58.770
- You can tell?
- Don't let it get to your head.

08:58.770 --> 09:02.000
You still have a way
to go if that excites you.

09:02.000 --> 09:05.670
What, you could at
least compliment me a bit!

09:05.670 --> 09:07.330
Hibiki?

09:09.240 --> 09:11.850
I experienced a lot on this trip.

09:11.850 --> 09:14.680
I've fought and met all kinds of people.

09:14.680 --> 09:17.720
No! Stop the footage from leaking out!

09:17.720 --> 09:19.750
This has never happened before!

09:19.750 --> 09:21.960
Of course!

09:21.960 --> 09:23.860
We're starting something new!

09:23.860 --> 09:26.390
There isn't a case like this anywhere!

09:26.390 --> 09:28.700
Everyone's doing everything they can!

09:28.700 --> 09:31.300
You guys aren't any more special!

09:31.300 --> 09:33.130
Don't hide in the corner barking...

09:33.130 --> 09:36.840
If you have time for that,
then come forward!

09:36.840 --> 09:38.810
Stand on your own stage!

09:38.810 --> 09:42.340
It's our future and no one else's!

09:42.340 --> 09:46.380
It's a future that we'll make
for ourselves with our own hands!

09:46.380 --> 09:48.380
How can we leave it to others?

09:48.380 --> 09:50.550
Don't lose! Don't give up!

09:50.550 --> 09:52.420
No matter how unsatisfied...

09:52.420 --> 09:54.520
No matter how unfair...

09:54.520 --> 09:57.390
What you see in front
of your eyes is everything.

09:57.390 --> 10:00.490
What can you see
if you turn your face away?

10:00.490 --> 10:04.630
What can you talk about without
overcoming the harsh reality?

10:04.630 --> 10:07.070
There needs to be a reason to live!

10:07.070 --> 10:09.590
You don't need an excuse to die!

10:11.770 --> 10:13.910
We can't shut our mouths.

10:13.910 --> 10:15.540
We can't end it.

10:15.540 --> 10:17.710
Right, Mr. Alien?

10:17.710 --> 10:19.380
I'm gonna fight!

10:19.380 --> 10:21.980
To keep the stream of life going!

10:21.980 --> 10:26.350
Oh, he hasn't done anything,
but it's picking everyone up.

10:26.350 --> 10:30.160
Paksis, you'll fight with us too, right?

10:30.160 --> 10:31.350
Let's go!

10:32.760 --> 10:34.630
We need to attack first!

10:34.630 --> 10:36.290
Combine!

10:40.640 --> 10:43.140
Has he no shame?

10:43.140 --> 10:44.240
Magno...

10:44.240 --> 10:48.570
I think I understand why
you told me to look around.

10:54.450 --> 10:55.420
Captain.

10:55.420 --> 10:57.350
Rebecca's Paraiso is approaching.

10:57.350 --> 11:00.350
Go back to the hideout, you all.

11:00.350 --> 11:01.690
I can't do that.

11:01.690 --> 11:05.730
I'll be yelled at later for
leaving an elderly person behind.

11:05.730 --> 11:11.170
Looks like you've grown
to speak insolently while I was gone.

11:11.170 --> 11:13.660
Things change when you become a parent.

11:16.470 --> 11:19.130
The Ikazuchi and
a pirate ship have made contact.

11:21.610 --> 11:26.140
All ships, attack formation alpha
with Vandread Dita in the center.

11:28.720 --> 11:31.020
Valore, the enemy's very agile.

11:31.020 --> 11:32.820
It's best to stay back.

11:32.820 --> 11:36.390
Oh, since when could
you talk to me like that?

11:36.390 --> 11:37.830
That's right!

11:37.830 --> 11:41.280
You haven't seen our skills in a while,
so I'd like to show them off!

11:46.630 --> 11:48.070
Barnette!

11:48.070 --> 11:50.000
There'll be deli orders anyway.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.670
Being here's the same thing.

11:51.670 --> 11:54.310
Or is it that you're itching to fight?

11:54.310 --> 11:56.870
Even stagehands can do this.

12:00.950 --> 12:03.520
Unidentified, giant battleship!

12:03.520 --> 12:06.210
Are we supposed to fight that?

12:07.890 --> 12:12.590
Giant object approaching
the Nirvana from 6 o'clock!

12:12.590 --> 12:15.200
Object identified as a harvest flagship.

12:15.200 --> 12:16.160
Why?

12:16.160 --> 12:18.270
It couldn't have appeared so suddenly!

12:18.270 --> 12:21.800
It's because the
Nirvana's ID code has been read...

12:21.800 --> 12:24.170
which slowed down identification!

12:24.170 --> 12:25.830
Nasty bunch.

12:28.080 --> 12:29.880
Barnette!

12:29.880 --> 12:32.080
I'll take the point and rush in!

12:32.080 --> 12:35.020
Still as hasty as ever, Barnette.

12:35.020 --> 12:37.250
Didn't I tell you it was a bad habit?

12:39.990 --> 12:42.090
T-That voice...

12:42.090 --> 12:43.750
Ms. Gasco?

12:45.460 --> 12:47.560
Then that was Ms. Gasco?

12:47.560 --> 12:49.700
That's why it knew our ID code!

12:49.700 --> 12:53.400
Jeez, it's not Gasco. It's Gascogne!

12:53.400 --> 12:55.800
That's definitely Ms. Gasco!

12:55.800 --> 12:57.970
I'm impressed she made it back...

12:57.970 --> 13:00.710
I thought it'd be
bad to come empty-handed...

13:00.710 --> 13:04.510
But the souvenir's big,
and that's why I'm a little late.

13:04.510 --> 13:08.180
I was getting this thing's
self-repair system fixed up.

13:08.180 --> 13:10.840
It's pretty cute once you tame it.

13:13.490 --> 13:15.150
Welcome back!

13:20.190 --> 13:21.960
Good job running things.

13:21.960 --> 13:25.020
I've got it from here, so go mix it up.

13:30.140 --> 13:31.540
Well then...

13:31.540 --> 13:33.200
Ms. Gasco...

13:34.440 --> 13:38.380
Thanks for staying alive.

13:39.950 --> 13:41.420
Sorry to make you wait!

13:41.420 --> 13:43.720
It's been a while since I've mixed it up!

13:43.720 --> 13:46.790
Barnette! You look much better that way!

13:46.790 --> 13:51.990
Hey! I heard there's
some big show around here.

13:51.990 --> 13:53.790
Rabat?

13:53.790 --> 13:58.390
Thanks to the markers you laid,
there's plenty of spectators here!

14:00.570 --> 14:04.140
Another fleet is approaching
fast behind Rabat's fleet!

14:04.140 --> 14:05.800
Another fleet?

14:07.470 --> 14:10.280
This is the anti-Earth fleet of Melanus!

14:10.280 --> 14:14.320
We've come to show our
friendship for Hibiki Tokai!

14:14.320 --> 14:15.780
Melanus...

14:15.780 --> 14:19.790
That's the star that was
Earth's target for harvesting skin.

14:19.790 --> 14:22.220
The squadron that saved Hibiki all died.

14:22.220 --> 14:25.460
They're inheriting their
friends' parting wills, huh...

14:25.460 --> 14:29.260
This is the Todoroki,
former flagship of a Tarak fleet.

14:29.260 --> 14:31.370
We agree with your intentions.

14:31.370 --> 14:33.930
Permission to join forces.

14:33.930 --> 14:35.270
Excuse me!

14:35.270 --> 14:38.670
I'm general of Gale Squadron's
attack Van-types

14:38.670 --> 14:40.510
Ozeki Kyunmel!

14:40.510 --> 14:43.810
We'd like the honor
of being the first to attack!

14:45.480 --> 14:47.910
Men are all so dumb!

14:49.080 --> 14:51.250
This is the Mejale Coast Guard!

14:51.250 --> 14:54.090
Is there some way we can help, as well?

14:54.090 --> 14:57.290
Wow, they're coming one after another!

15:02.230 --> 15:05.900
So many are coming to aid Hibiki's call...

15:05.900 --> 15:10.800
I guess it really is out of our hands...

15:10.800 --> 15:12.210
Response from marker!

15:12.210 --> 15:14.980
Giant objects confirmed,
and they're moving!

15:14.980 --> 15:17.070
They've finally come.

15:20.980 --> 15:23.970
The harvest fleet has
gotten past the magnetic storm!

15:31.790 --> 15:33.450
What?

15:51.750 --> 15:53.470
Fakes again!

15:56.320 --> 15:59.720
Interesting! This is a good day to die!

16:01.920 --> 16:03.580
No way!

16:10.860 --> 16:13.370
Everyone, follow me!

16:13.370 --> 16:14.340
Amazing...

16:14.340 --> 16:16.170
We can't lose now!

16:25.480 --> 16:26.850
Commence attack!

16:26.850 --> 16:28.180
Roger!

16:32.450 --> 16:34.350
Well, here goes!

16:49.870 --> 16:50.870
Damn it!

16:50.870 --> 16:53.570
Dodge if it's going to hit you!

16:59.110 --> 17:02.170
Whoa, this is another extravagant one!

17:04.650 --> 17:06.310
Not yet...

17:17.600 --> 17:19.900
You're in the way!

17:31.610 --> 17:34.480
The same tactic won't work again!

17:34.480 --> 17:36.140
Yeah!

17:45.590 --> 17:46.960
Leader! Valore!

17:46.960 --> 17:50.230
You're still a headache, huh?

17:50.230 --> 17:53.000
You've gotten a harsher tongue, Valore.

17:53.000 --> 17:54.370
Did you just laugh?

17:54.370 --> 17:57.200
We're no longer who we used to be.

17:57.200 --> 17:59.540
Because of the men?

17:59.540 --> 18:01.680
Oh, I don't know.

18:01.680 --> 18:03.440
Doze off and I'll leave you behind!

18:03.440 --> 18:04.710
That's what it means.

18:04.710 --> 18:07.310
What's up with this?

18:07.310 --> 18:08.750
Forget the weak ones.

18:08.750 --> 18:11.270
- We'll go straight to the flagship
- All right!

18:15.120 --> 18:17.060
No way! Even Meia?

18:17.060 --> 18:20.190
The coolest one is still
in the wings so just wait.

18:20.190 --> 18:22.360
And who used to say it was the worst?

18:22.360 --> 18:24.350
- Shut up.
- Sorry.

18:26.070 --> 18:30.140
They still have breathing room.
It's as if they're enjoying this.

18:30.140 --> 18:32.270
Something's changed.

18:32.270 --> 18:36.710
There's something new in the
crew that's different from before...

18:38.310 --> 18:40.110
I'm looking forward to the future.

18:53.360 --> 18:56.400
You were all the way here?
That's too reckless, old man.

18:56.400 --> 18:57.660
Don't make me laugh!

18:57.660 --> 19:00.530
I don't have a strange
machine like you do...

19:00.530 --> 19:03.830
but I have techniques that
I've been perfecting over the years!

19:05.040 --> 19:09.180
Don't perish until you learn to survive.

19:09.180 --> 19:10.280
Go!

19:10.280 --> 19:11.940
Yeah!

19:20.220 --> 19:21.880
Hibiki...

19:25.090 --> 19:26.930
I feel it...

19:26.930 --> 19:29.260
We're definitely getting closer!

19:30.960 --> 19:34.940
A giant object is confirmed
moving past the magnetic storm!

19:34.940 --> 19:37.770
- What?
- The main one is here!

19:37.770 --> 19:39.770
That's not a harvest flagship.

19:39.770 --> 19:43.010
That's the monster that destroys
planets they no longer need!

19:43.010 --> 19:44.670
The main one?

19:47.110 --> 19:49.340
Do your best, Paksis.

19:54.620 --> 19:55.560
That's...

19:55.560 --> 19:56.920
That's the main one?

19:56.920 --> 19:58.690
Then it's a quick deal!

19:58.690 --> 20:00.350
Let's go!

20:04.230 --> 20:05.570
Whoa, it's ugly!

20:05.570 --> 20:07.070
Shut up!

20:07.070 --> 20:09.700
Everyone, follow us! We'll break through!

20:09.700 --> 20:11.360
Roger!

20:17.280 --> 20:18.940
All ships, turn around!

20:24.280 --> 20:25.920
Jura, are you all right?

20:25.920 --> 20:28.490
- Somehow...
- Damn you!

20:28.490 --> 20:30.720
It's time for Vandread Pyoro!

20:30.720 --> 20:32.260
Don't give it a weird name!

20:32.260 --> 20:33.920
Why?

20:59.390 --> 21:01.620
Don't get in our way!

21:12.630 --> 21:14.290
Is that it?

21:19.010 --> 21:21.940
We've found it! The scariest one!
